              <div class="faq__answer">
                Nail Bite Beaver sits in your Mac menu bar and monitors for nail
                biting/face touching behaviour. It detects this using the
                built-in functionality on all Mac devices called “CoreML” (see
                further technical details below). It gives the behaviour a
                score, and the closer to a 100, the further out the beaver will
                appear until it eventually covers your whole screen, forcing you
                to stop. The goal is that it stops you before you even get to
                the point of biting.
              </div>
